# Shell scripts and files they source keep LF on every checkout. Git for Windows
# converts to CRLF by default (core.autocrlf), and bash stops at the first `\r`: the
# standalone build would fail on a Windows runner, the checksums it reads from the
# lock would end in `\r`, and the install.sh it copies into the release would break
# the installer for every macOS and Linux user.
*.sh text eol=lf
scripts/agent_browser.lock text eol=lf
